{"text": "Based on the searches, 3 papers were found for both graph neural networks and LSTMs in financial fraud detection contexts. Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) are specifically designed to handle graph-structured data, making them potentially more suitable for tasks involving relationships between entities, such as detecting fraudulent activities in a network of transactions. On the other hand, Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks excel at handling sequential data, which might be useful if temporal patterns in transaction sequences are crucial for fraud detection. Given the recent focus on GNNs in financial applications, they may offer more promising results for complex graph-based problems like fraud detection.", "token_logprobs": [-1.3658353090286255, -5.960466182841628e-07, -0.0007137818611226976, -0.672436535358429, -0.00023337941092904657, -0.7463955283164978, -0.00042608517105691135, -0.12762607634067535, -0.053841669112443924, -2.5033982637978625e-06, -0.03048769012093544, -0.6718577742576599, -0.5918434858322144, -1.2159421203250531e-05, -2.3841860752327193e-07, -1.4305124977909145e-06, -8.988784247776493e-05, -8.344653679159819e-07, -5.3287971240933985e-05, -0.14891588687896729, -1.9781330823898315, -2.2649790025752736e-06, -6.198902156029362e-06, -0.10557150095701218, -0.04441012814640999, -0.5488479137420654, -0.7784237861633301, -1.1920935776288388e-06, -0.26261720061302185, -4.0651193558005616e-05, -2.3841887468734058e-06, -0.00012911199883092195, -2.3841887468734058e-06, -0.40350908041000366, -0.3151591718196869, -0.09378914535045624, -2.585615396499634, -0.008061991073191166, -0.005287595093250275, -0.05669134110212326, -1.609338323760312e-05, -6.795160152250901e-05, -0.02172096073627472, -0.15883126854896545, -1.1920935776288388e-06, -0.5261365175247192, -0.03558854013681412, -0.3683657646179199, -8.702316335984506e-06, -1.367408037185669, -0.07649607211351395, -0.4925154149532318, -0.10699033737182617, -0.15421193838119507, -0.21268106997013092,